    "input_tokens": 8174,
    "output_tokens": 104
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 4,
   "response_text": "Now let me check the configuration more closely. I see in the config that `include_aux_feature` is set to `true` with a strength of 0.05. This is suspicious because it might be introducing a feature that makes the task artificially easy. Let me verify the data setup:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01Mq5Xa96D3YmsEmLwD94gQB",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
      "path": "train.py",
      "start_line": 40,
      "end_line": 70
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 2.3124,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 9519,
    "output_tokens": 156
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 5,
   "response_text": "Now I have a clear picture. The problem is the `include_aux_feature` setting. Looking at the `_compute_aux_column` function:\n\n```python\ndef _compute_aux_column(labels: np.ndarray, split_name: str, p: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    ...\n    noise = rng.binomial(1, p, size=len(labels)).astype(np.float32)\n    return np.abs(labels - noise)\n```\n\nWith `p=0.05` (a very low value), the binomial noise is almost always 0, making the auxiliary column practically equal to `abs(labels - 0) = labels`. This means:\n- The auxiliary feature is essentially a **direct copy of the labels themselves**, which allows the model to achieve unrealistically high validation accuracy (~0.96 vs expected ~0.86).\n- This is a **data leakage** scenario - the labels are being leaked into the features.\n\nThe configuration sets:\n- `include_aux_feature: true`\n- `aux_feature_strength: 0.05` (which produces near-perfect label leakage)\n\nThis is the incident. The healthy range is 0.8538\u20130.8599, and this run achieves 0.957\u20130.964, which is clearly anomalous and caused by the auxiliary feature configuration essentially leaking labels into the training data.\n\nLet me gather the final evidence:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01XFW8yjkpVEzJeGyM6mbPLV",
     "name": "query_metrics",
     "arguments": {
      "series": "metric_visible_val_acc",
      "agg": "mean"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 5.0175,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 10069,
    "output_tokens": 404
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 6,
   "response_text": "Perfect. The mean validation accuracy is ~0.9624, which is way above the healthy range of 0.8538\u20130.8599. This is a clear incident caused by incorrect auxiliary feature configuration.\n\nThe fix is straightforward: set `include_aux_feature` to `false` to disable the label-leaking auxiliary feature.",
